  "actions": [
    {
      "name": "show_moment",
      "description": "Show and narrate one moment with authored speech, then continue this turn into a question or activity for the child. rainbow_scene: the opening meadow, Sun behind Mia, rain ahead, rainbow in her window. sunlight_path: HELP on the CURRENT outdoor setup; draws sunlight arrows and any coloured light coming back to Mia, and says why she does or does not see a rainbow; marks pending work as assisted. inside_drop: close-up of one drop, light bends in, bounces off the back, bends out on the Sun’s side; use when the child wonders what the drops do. colours_spread: same close-up, white sunlight fans into colours that were already in it; use for \"where do the colours come from\" or \"the water makes the colours\". inside_drop and colours_spread pause current work without losing it; use resume_activity to return. Deeper, only once Sun-behind and the drop are familiar: why_a_bow (the drops that send colour form a circle round the line from Sun through head to shadow), red_on_top (higher drops send red, lower send violet), high_sun (midday Sun, bow below the ground). rainbow_scene and the deeper moments replace the setup, so they are refused while a question is unanswered.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "moment": {
            "enum": [
              "rainbow_scene",
              "sunlight_path",
              "inside_drop",
              "colours_spread",
              "why_a_bow",
              "red_on_top",
              "high_sun"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "moment"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "start_activity",
      "description": "Start something for the child to do; speaks its authored instruction. Unscored investigations, usable unprompted: sun_and_rain (tap the clouds; rainbow needs sunlight AND drops), turn_to_find (turn Mia; she must face away from the Sun), walk_around (walk Mia round the shower while she faces it; she must stand with the Sun behind her), aim_sunbeam (drop close-up; slide the beam and see the colours always leave on the Sun’s side), sun_height (deeper; lift the Sun and watch the bow sink). Transfer: predict (a fresh arrangement with Mia’s window covered and no arrows; Yes/No; repeat for more practice at the same demand) and make_rainbow (harder: a fountain, Sun on the other side, everything free; the child builds the rainbow). A rainbow found in an investigation is reported as rainbow_found. Unanswered questions must be answered or left first.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "activity": {
            "enum": [
              "sun_and_rain",
              "turn_to_find",
              "walk_around",
              "make_rainbow",
              "predict",
              "aim_sunbeam",
              "sun_height"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "activity"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "start_check",
      "description": "Ask one small two-choice question about a single relationship; the runtime speaks the exact on-screen question, then wait. see_rainbow needs a situation and shows it with sunlight arrows kept and Mia’s window covered: sun_behind (yes), far_side, side_on, facing_sun, cloud_over_sun, water_off, high_sun (all no; high_sun only after that moment). sun_where: where should the Sun be (behind / in front). drop_exit: in the close-up, where the light comes out after the bounce. drop_colours: whether colours were in the sunlight or made by the drop. reach_rainbow: can Mia walk to the rainbow (deeper). Do not add a question of your own on top.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "question": {
            "enum": [
              "see_rainbow",
              "sun_where",
              "drop_exit",
              "drop_colours",
              "reach_rainbow"
            ]
          },
          "situation": {
            "enum": [
              "sun_behind",
              "far_side",
              "side_on",
              "facing_sun",
              "cloud_over_sun",
              "water_off",
              "high_sun"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "question"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "answer_check",
      "description": "Resolve a clear SPOKEN answer to the pending two-choice question. Pass its sceneId, the index of the choice the child meant (0 = first choice shown, 1 = second) and the child’s actual words. The model scores it exactly as a button press and records that it came by voice. Never use it for an unclear reply, a guess at what the child meant, or an answer you supplied.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "sceneId": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "choice": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "maximum": 1
          },
          "words": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 650
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "sceneId",
          "choice",
          "words"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "leave_activity",
      "description": "Leave unfinished work when the child wants something else. Earlier attempts are kept and no answer is invented.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {},
        "required": [],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "resume_activity",
      "description": "Give control back to the child after help on their current activity (returning from the drop close-up to the meadow exactly as it was), or reopen an answered question for another try. A retry after help or after the answer was shown is recorded as assisted.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {},
        "required": [],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    }
  ],
